1.Arrays or more accurately static arrays, have a fixed size.
  so if we don't know the size we should use linkedList (or dynamic array like ArrayList)

Note: dynamic arrays grow by 50%  (Arraylist)
                     grow by 100% (Vector)
      so they waste some memory.

Note: linked-list use memory as mush he really need!
      but he need some extra memory on each node
      to store next node reference.
      SO HE HASE BIGGER FOOTPRINT THAN ARRAYS!


    +------------------------+-----------+-------------+
    | Operation              | Array     | Linked List |
    +------------------------+-----------+-------------+
    | Lookup by index        | O(1)      | O(n)        |
    | Lookup by value        | O(n)      | O(n)        |
    | Insert at beginning    | O(n)      | O(1)        |        Note: we use linked list on heavy insert app
    | Insert at end          | O(n)      | O(1)        |              it's so fast to add item at the ned!
    | Insert in middle       | O(n)      | O(n)        |
    | Delete at beginning    | O(n)      | O(1)        |        Note: we use Arrays when we want to fine item
    | Delete in middle       | O(n)      | O(n)        |              based on index.
    | Delete at end          | O(1)      | O(n)        |
    +------------------------+-----------+-------------+